==English==

===Etymology===
From {{inh|en|enm|semyngly}}, equivalent to {{af|en|seeming|-ly|id2=adverbial}}.

===Pronunciation===
* {{IPA|en|/ˈsiːmɪŋli/}}
* {{audio|en|en-us-seemingly.ogg|a=US}}
* {{hyph|en|seem|ing|ly}}

===Adverb===
{{en-adv}}

# As it appears; [[apparently]].
#* {{quote-book|en|year=1748|author=David Hume|title=Enquiries concerning the human understanding and concerning the principles of moral|publisher=Oxford University Press|year_published=1973|others=section 15|passage={{...}} an object, '''seemingly''' like those which we have experienced, may be attended with different or contrary effects.}}
#* {{quote-book|en|year=1816|author=w:Jane Austen|title=[[w:Emma (novel)|Emma]]|volume=1|chapter=8|passage=Mr. Woodhouse at last was off; but Mr. Knightley, instead of being immediately off likewise, sat down again, '''seemingly''' inclined for more chat. He began speaking of Harriet, and speaking of her with more voluntary praise than Emma had ever heard before.}}
#* {{RQ:Maxwell Mirror and the Lamp|chapter=5|passage=Then everybody once more knelt, and soon the blessing was pronounced. The choir and the clergy trooped out slowly, {{...}}, down the nave to the western door. {{...}} At a '''seemingly''' immense distance the surpliced group stopped to say the last prayer.}}
#* {{quote-book|en|year=2006|author=Ace Collins|title=More Stories Behind the Best-Loved Songs of Christmas|pageurl=http://books.google.com/books?id=AWRr-nXbQDYC&pg=PA64&dq=%22more%7Cmost+seemingly%22&hl=en&ei=c5iITsm4HeyTiAeTuP2GDw&sa=X&oi=book_result&ct=result&resnum=9&sqi=2&ved=0CFIQ6AEwCA#v=onepage&q=%22more%7Cmost%20seemingly%22&f=false|page=64|passage=He sacrificed nothing, laboring to get even the most '''seemingly''' insignificant element of every record perfect.}}
#* {{quote-journal|en|date=2011-10-01|author=Tom Fordyce|title=Rugby World Cup 2011: England 16-12 Scotland|work=BBC Sport|url=http://news.bbc.co.uk/sport2/hi/rugby_union/15124512.stm|page=|passage=With rain lashing across the ground at kick-off and every man in Auckland '''seemingly''' either English-born or supporting Scotland, Eden Park was transformed into Murrayfield in March.}}
# In a [[seemly]] manner; [[decorously]]; with [[propriety]].
#* {{quote-book|en|year=1950|author=Francis Charles Turner|title=James II|pageurl=http://books.google.com/books?id=GVgDAAAAMAAJ&q=%22behave%7Cbehaves%7Cbehaved%7Cbehaving+seemingly%22&dq=%22behave%7Cbehaves%7Cbehaved%7Cbehaving+seemingly%22&hl=en&ei=vpSITvC0Csy0iQfhudmhDw&sa=X&oi=book_result&ct=result&resnum=1&ved=0CCsQ6AEwADg8|page=172|passage=It was possibly chagrin at this neglect that caused James to omit the most ordinary courtesies to the few gentlemen who had behaved '''seemingly''':{{...}}.}}
#* {{quote-book|en|year=1974|author=G[odfrey] N[wanoruo] Uzoigwe|title=Britain and the Conquest of Africa: The Age of Salisbury|pageurl=http://books.google.com/books?id=AN9xAAAAMAAJ&q=%22behave%7Cbehaves%7Cbehaved%7Cbehaving+seemingly%22&dq=%22behave%7Cbehaves%7Cbehaved%7Cbehaving+seemingly%22&hl=en&ei=vpSITvC0Csy0iQfhudmhDw&sa=X&oi=book_result&ct=result&resnum=2&ved=0CC8Q6AEwATg8|page=180|passage={{...}}was restored to his throne but only on the understanding that he behave '''seemingly'''.}}
#* {{quote-book|en|year=1989|author=Yi-fu Tuan|title=Morality & Imagination: Paradoxes of Progress|pageurl=http://books.google.com/books?id=MhiIuDmoxQMC&pg=PA40&dq=%22behave%7Cbehaves%7Cbehaved%7Cbehaving+seemingly%22&hl=en&ei=kpGITrWkJ9CdiAePq-3_Ag&sa=X&oi=book_result&ct=result&resnum=1&ved=0CCsQ6AEwADgU#v=onepage&q=%22behave%7Cbehaves%7Cbehaved%7Cbehaving%20seemingly%22&f=false|page=40|passage={{...}}they know the roles and statuses of deities, ancestral spirits, and men, and how to behave '''seemingly''' in their presence.}}

